.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_RAND-JITTER 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_RAND-JITTER
.Nd The randomness seed source EVP_RAND implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for deterministic random number generator seeding through the
.Sy EVP_RAND
API.
.Pp
This software seed source produces randomness based on tiny CPU "jitter"
fluctuations.
.Pp
It is available when OpenSSL is compiled with
.Sy enable-jitter
option.
When available it is listed in
.Sy openssl list -random-generators
and
.Sy openssl info -seeds .
.Ss Identity
"JITTER" is the name for this implementation; it can be used with the
.Xr EVP_RAND_fetch 3
function.
.Ss Supported parameters
The supported parameters are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqstate" ( Ns Sy OSSL_RAND_PARAM_STATE Ns ) <integer>
.It \(dqstrength" ( Ns Sy OSSL_RAND_PARAM_STRENGTH Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqmax_request" ( Ns Sy OSSL_RAND_PARAM_MAX_REQUEST Ns ) <unsigned integer>
These parameters work as described in
.Xr EVP_RAND 3 .
.El
.Sh NOTES
A context for the seed source can be obtained by calling:
.Bd -literal
 EVP_RAND *rand = EVP_RAND_fetch(NULL, "JITTER", NULL);
 EVP_RAND_CTX *rctx = EVP_RAND_CTX_new(rand, NULL);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Sy enable-jitter
option was added in OpenSSL 3.4.
.Pp
By specifying the
.Sy enable-fips-jitter
configuration option, the FIPS provider will use an internal jitter
source for its entropy.
Enabling this option will cause the FIPS provider to operate in a
non-compliant mode unless an entropy assessment
.Lk https://csrc.nist.gov/Projects/cryptographic-module-validation-program/entropy-validations
and validation through the
.Lk https://csrc.nist.gov/projects/cryptographic-module-validation-program
are additionally conducted.
This option was added in OpenSSL 3.5.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
 EVP_RAND *rand;
 EVP_RAND_CTX *seed, *rctx;
 unsigned char bytes[100];
 OSSL_PARAM params[2], *p = params;
 unsigned int strength = 128;

 /* Create and instantiate a seed source */
 rand = EVP_RAND_fetch(NULL, "JITTER", NULL);
 seed = EVP_RAND_CTX_new(rand, NULL);
 EVP_RAND_instantiate(seed, strength, 0, NULL, 0, NULL);
 EVP_RAND_free(rand);

 /* Feed this into a DRBG */
 rand = EVP_RAND_fetch(NULL, "CTR-DRBG", NULL);
 rctx = EVP_RAND_CTX_new(rand, seed);
 EVP_RAND_free(rand);

 /* Configure the DRBG */
 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_utf8_string(OSSL_DRBG_PARAM_CIPHER,
                                         SN_aes_256_ctr, 0);
 *p = OSSL_PARAM_construct_end();
 EVP_RAND_instantiate(rctx, strength, 0, NULL, 0, params);

 EVP_RAND_generate(rctx, bytes, sizeof(bytes), strength, 0, NULL, 0);

 EVP_RAND_CTX_free(rctx);
 EVP_RAND_CTX_free(seed);
.Ed
